<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ma'an</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Maan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ma'an is a city in southern Jordan on the old caravan and pilgrimage route between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hejaz">Hejaz</a>, later served by the Hejaz Railway. In November 1920 Abdullah, son of Sharif Husayn of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mecca">Mecca</a>, arrived there with his followers, the first step towards founding the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a> of Transjordan. It is the capital of the Ma'an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/governorate">Governorate</a>, which includes <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petra">Petra</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/maan-jordan.jpg" alt="Ma'an" width="320" height="358" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: American Colony (Jerusalem). Photo Dept. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Petra-Locomotive.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
